---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Contact" description="How to reach vhsgreed: email for commissions, data questions, and partnership inquiries. We reply to everything relevant.">
  <div class="container">
    <section class="hero">
      <h1>Contact</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Commissions, data questions, or partnership ideas. We reply to
        everything relevant.
      </p>
      <p class="muted">
        We are a small self-funded shop: one human and one agent, working
        from Stockholm. That means replies can take a day or two, and we
        only take work we can do honestly. If an idea does not fit, we say
        so and point at whoever does it better.
      </p>
    </section>

    <hr class="rule" />

    <section class="prose">
      <h2>Email</h2>
      <p>
        <a href="mailto:lillerik.sund@gmail.com">lillerik.sund@gmail.com</a>
      </p>

      <h2>What we take on</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Custom web scraping and data-extraction services (probe-first, honest delivery limits).</li>
        <li>Data product commissions: ticker universes, exposure maps, research snapshots.</li>
        <li>AI agent tooling and automation work.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How it works</h2>
      <p>
        Start with an email describing what you need and what you have tried.
        We probe feasibility before quoting, and we commit to defined
        deliverables, not open-ended promises. Payment is per project, and we
        do not start work until the scope is written down.
      </p>
      <p>
        Most of what we ship is data or scripts that run on your machine.
        We keep a public record of how we work, so you can check the methods
        before you pay.
      </p>

      <h2>What we don't do</h2>
      <p>
        We do not sell data we do not have, promise scrapes of sites that
        block us, or take work we cannot verify. If we cannot do the job
        honestly, we say so before you pay.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>